  "chapter": 356,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 6 Chapter 356\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 7155, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to crediting of\n        probationary service\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation requires that when a public  employee  moves  from  a\nprovisional  title to a permanent title, all time served by the employee\nin the provisional title counts  toward  any  probationary  time  period\nrequired for the permanent position.\n \n  Public employees who have worked in a provisional title and are placed\nin a permanent position have demonstrated that they have performed their\njob  duties  as  employees and deserve the full protections of the Civil\nService Law. I agree with the legislative intent of this bill and  fully\nsupport  extending  these  protections  to  workers under the conditions\ndescribed by the sponsors.\n \n  The bill required technical changes to clarify who is eligible for the\nprotections described in the bill. I have secured an agreement with  the\nLegislature  to  clarify that the permanent position must be immediately\nfollowing the provisional position. In light of  this  agreement,  I  am\npleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
